        &nbsp;<a href="post.asp?method=TopicQuote&TOPIC_ID=913&FORUM_ID=4&CAT_ID=1&Forum_Title=The+Round+Table&Topic_Title=Dear+Lore+Keepers%2E%2E%2E"><img src="icon_reply_topic.gif" height=15 width=15 alt="Reply with Quote" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>

        <hr noshade size="1">
        
        <font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"> Dear Lore Keepers,</P><P>It is with great sadness that I have decided to leave the Lore Keepers.  I fear my actions have caused us to loose a member of our guild.  Though normally I would not go into the details, I feel I must.  This is the only way I can apologize and ensure it is understood the apology is sincere.</P><P>A couple of weeks ago I was conversing with a friend.  During that conversation I accidentally said “Vulcana and Valimar, not two of my favorite LK’ers right now” in guild say.  Though the statement was accurate; however it was not meant for public consumption.  I was not happy with either player and was extremely frustrated and am now over it.  </P><P>Valimar.  </P><P>Twice I had asked Valimar to assist me in a resurrection.  The last time was earlier the day of the statement.  I had died to a bug in EQ, had to go back to work and was going to exceed the three hour time limit on exp ress’es.  Though only two zones (one real small one) away Valimar explained he was busy and could not help.  I was already frustrated, and had proven myself to be willing to assist Valimar on more that one occasion even when it was not convenient. A specific example had occurred a few days prior.  I had just passed through GD and received a tell from Val.  He had asked if I could solo Frost Giants?  I said sure, there blue, it wouldn’t be a problem.  Would I help him kill some?  With out question, I told the group I was going to, that I would not be there. I didn’t even explain to Val, I had not made a decision at that time that about my Giant/Coldain faction. I dropped everything I had to do and went to help out a guild mate.</P><P>I have since spoken with Valimar asking him to reconsider his decision to leave LK. He is (was) a valuable member of the guild and I am sorry he decided to leave.  I was surprised to hear he had spoken with an officer in the guild who had agreed the player balance would not be upset by Val’s departure.  </P><P>Vulcana</P><P>Recently I won the roll on a nice robe.  Good AC among other things and light weight.  Vulcana had shouted in guild say that she was looking for the same robe.  I spoke with the group I had been playing with at the time and asked for permission to give the robe to her.  I was able to get the permission I was looking for and told Vul. I had a robe for her.  But that the robe was with another character who was trying to sell it.  Over the next couple of weeks I receive a couple of tells from Vul. “Where’s so and so, I want my robe”(paraphrased).  I almost decided not to give it to her, but my conscience got the better of me.  So I asked the person to go ahead and give her the robe.  After the exchange took place the person who had the robe informed me the robe had been delivered.  So a few minutes pass, no “hey nice robe, thanks” from Vul.  And hour passes, then two.  I have gotten a little frustrated at that point with the ingratitude being displayed.   So I send a tell.  “Hey, want to check, did you get the robe”  “Yes, I got the robe” is the reply.  Still no Hey thanks for the 1200pp robe, I appreciate it. Nothing.  Sorry, I don’t do stuff for thanks, but I do expect guild mates to be polite to each other.</P><P>Anyway, my friends my actions have caused at least on member of the guild to leave.  “Kenton won’t be sorry to see me leave” was I think the term used by Vulcana last night.  I don’t think Valimar’s leaving can be placed on my shoulders.  At least I hope not. He was already gone by the time I goofed and slipped in Guild Say.</P><P>I am deeply sorry for any offense I may have caused.  Please accept my apology.</P><P><BR>Kenton Cuttahotha<BR>Druid of the 45th Life Ring<BR>Do Not Meddle in the Affairs of Dragons... For you are Crunchy and Taste Good with Ketchup!!!</font></td>
