        <font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"> I have to agree with Spuff that browso is an excellent leader, from his actions thus far and I also agree with browso that an effective leader must have the communication of his guild in order for him to be more useful and he's right that how can he fix things if he doesn't know what's going on.  I would certainly be frustrated if things just fall through my fingers and I don't seem to know why or even try to stop it.  </P><P>The better we are informed about a sitatuation the better we can handle things and the only way we can be better informed is if we communicate what's going on.  LK is going through a turbulent time and I think it's time to actually put everything on the floor with some sort of guild meeting to discuss thing and esp in light of the recent move logs we will actually know who has stayed and who has gone.</P><P>I implore every remain LK'er to think about what has been done in the past and what has been said and hopefully if guild meeting is set up and we discuss our problems we can pave the way to some sort of resolution</P><P>Kenton, in light of what has been said thus far, the two that have left is in certainly no way your fault before you do that guild remove please think about what has happened.</P><P>Abyn<BR>Magician of the 51st circle</P><P></P><P>Edited by - Abyn on 21 Mar 2001  13:50:17<a href="#top"><img src="icon_go_up.gif" height=15 width=15 border="0" align="right" alt="Go to Top of Page"></a></font></td>
