        <hr noshade size="1">
        
        <font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"> Kenton,</P><P>Leaving the guild will in no way improve things for either yourself, or for the guild as a whole.  I beg you to reconsider.</P><P>It was Vulcana's choice to leave the guild, and it was very odd.  She stated her reason in guildchat, she was bored of EQ.  I've spent the past week watching her ask people for favors and saw many people willing to help her.  Yet she left last night with no notice at all, just decided she was tired of the game.  I don't think you need concern yourself with her actions.</P><P>As for Valimar, I can understand why he left.  Because of his level, he was unable to really group with any of his guildmates, and it was probably disheartening.  I doubt his decision was affected much by your disagreement.</P><P>Guys, everyone has disagreements, and there is no better way to clear them up than communcating as a guild.  I have shared Browso's surprise by finding out that our members have been leaving when I spot their name tag with another guild at the end.  It is very disturbing that they gave zero notice, and nobody knew of their departure.</P><P>If anyone has a problem with the guild, PLEASE let an officer know.  Post it on the board, so something!  Communication is good.</P><P>Ealadan Azurefire<BR>Keeper of Tears<BR>Eyes of Tunare</P><P>Edited by - Ealadan Azurefire on 21 Mar 2001  14:20:37<a href="#top"><img src="icon_go_up.gif" height=15 width=15 border="0" align="right" alt="Go to Top of Page"></a></font></td>
