        <hr noshade size="1">
        
        <font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"> The Lore Keepers is more stable under Browso than it has ever been. I feel he is the best Leader LK has ever had. There are many different styles of leadership. Browso's style is very quiet, not pushy - he is ever the diplomat and the calm voice of reason. He will always be my friend - one of my best, actually - and I think more of him than just about anyone in this game. I respect him more than almost anyone I know. If he quits, my heart will break - and I will do anything to keep that from happening.<BR>I handled my leaving very poorly. I posted in the officers' section - and did not want to call attention to my leaving by posting here. That was stupid, but you know what they say about hindsight. &lt;sigh&gt;<BR>I spoke to him before I left - and planned to be guildless for a while. The invite from QA took me by surprise, but I played more with them than with anyone else recently, so I joined. <BR>I guess I am rambling, so I will try to make a point.<BR>I look around LK and I see amazing people, so much talent, many new names and faces who are really enthusiatic and have a great deal of drive. New blood is good, change is good. If we do not change we stagnate and die.<BR>Kenton, Valimar and Vulcana leaving has NOTHING to do with you.<BR>Some others who have left I do not understand - I just know my reasons and teggo's reasons. Neither had anything to do with any problems - I beleive we left on good terms and I actually play more with Lore keepers now than I did before - go figure that one out. &lt;shrugs&gt;</P><P>This is a good place to be. Have some faith in what you have.</P><P></P><P>Lling Satori<BR>"I ma tauntning!!! Sopt runnig!!1"<BR>	- Borce</P><P><a href="#top"><img src="icon_go_up.gif" height=15 width=15 border="0" align="right" alt="Go to Top of Page"></a></font></td>
