        <hr noshade size="1">
        
        <font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"> I have to echo Browso's question: WTF?<BR>And the idea "I can't fix it if I don't know what's wrong."</P><P>Look I'm on most every night.  In between shouting for groups, I'm paying pretty close attention to guild chat.  Of the list of people listed whom have left the guild, I had absolutely no idea they were either unhappy or thinking of departure.</P><P>Nobody is stating, hinting or dropping the faintest clue they're having a problem.  I came close, myself, almost a year ago, but I took an extended vacation and created Bruna.<BR>I was frustrated by a group of Lore Keepers with whom I had grouped who weren't communicating.  Now I'm getting frustrated by people popping up with "I'm leaving, bye!" </P><P>You know, this is like working with someone for months and suddenly they're not working there anymore.  Management doesn't say a thing, leading to all kinds of speculation.<BR>"I was just talking to X yesterday, everything was fine."</P><P>Bottom line: Talk to us, people! If it's not an RL problem, we can probably fix it--or work at it.  </P><P>BTW, my own take on some of this?<BR>Guild is still family for me.  Quitting without talking is like coming home to an empty house--with no note, no warning.</P><P>Look, if you've got a problem, talk to someone. Browso, Senina, any officer (if you can figure out who they are, you're a better human than I)...hell,  I'm almost always available--just give us a tell. We'll figure out something.  Email me if you must. <BR>These are two different accts I use daily, I'm either on one or the other most of the time.</P><P><a href="mailto:Sigfried99@aol.com">Sigfried99@aol.com</a><BR>or<BR>Geekasaurus <a href="mailto:Rex@aol.com">Rex@aol.com</a></P><P></P><P>Merilla Vanilla Cleric 41<BR>Not just a young-in anymore!<BR>"Um--You gonna loot that?"<a href="#top"><img src="icon_go_up.gif" height=15 width=15 border="0" align="right" alt="Go to Top of Page"></a></font></td>
